# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Node / Electron
node_modules/
dist/
out/
.vite/

# Local runtime state
/run/
/storage/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment overrides
.env
.env.local
ovs.local.toml

# Built here rather than shipped: the measurement FFmpeg (tools/build-ffmpeg.sh
# --profile openh264), the Windows installer electron-builder makes, and
# anything else a tool puts beside them.
/build/

# The client's own FFmpeg (tools/build-ffmpeg.sh --profile client). A hundred
# and fifty megabytes of binary that any machine can rebuild, and the release
# workflow does. Its absence is why `build.mjs` has something to say.
/clients/desktop/vendor/

# The whole of docs/, by the owner’s decision (2026-09-24). The product
# specification, the engineering notes, the decision records, the risk register
# and their own working documents: all of it stays beside this checkout and on
# the mirror, and none of it is published.
#
# reference/ is the exception and is not in here: FIXTURES.md and MODULES.md are
# generated from the code, verified by golden tests, and are what somebody
# programmes a lighting console from. They were never internal.
docs/

# A complete copy of the history as it stood before it was rewritten
# (2026-09-24), kept until the rewrite has been looked at and trusted.
# Restore from it with: git clone .git-backup-before-rewrite.bundle
.git-backup-before-rewrite.bundle

# The NDI SDK, which its licence calls Confidential Information and forbids
# disclosing to anybody outside this company. It currently sits under docs/ and
# is therefore already ignored — but by a rule about something else entirely,
# and a licence obligation should not rest on that. Named here so it stays out
# however docs/ is decided later.
**/NDISDK/
*NDI_SDK*
